{"schema":"mao-cross-channel-public-site-data/1","script":"0063","rows":[{"ref":"ccfc:sn:0063:00000039:text","row":15352,"ordinal":1,"kind":"text","jp":"「おい、反転属性つき勝ち気娘」","en":"“Hey, feisty girl with a built-in reverse mode.”","speakerJa":"太一","speakerEn":"Taichi","ghs":[{"id":"ghs-tl:finding:001977","unitId":"ghs-tl:cca0014a:00001","en":"Taichi: \"Hey, unyielding girl with the Reversible Character Attribute!\"","verdict":"acceptable","categories":["presentation"]}]},{"ref":"ccfc:sn:0063:000000f5:text","row":15353,"ordinal":2,"kind":"text","jp":"「はぁ……？」","en":"“Excuse me...?”","speakerJa":"冬子","speakerEn":"Touko","ghs":[{"id":"ghs-tl:finding:001978","unitId":"ghs-tl:cca0014a:00002","en":"Touko: \"Huh...?\"","verdict":"acceptable","categories":["presentation"]}]},{"ref":"ccfc:sn:0063:00000123:text","row":15354,"ordinal":3,"kind":"text","jp":"「これをやる」","en":"“Here. Take this.”","speakerJa":"太一","speakerEn":"Taichi","ghs":[{"id":"ghs-tl:finding:001979","unitId":"ghs-tl:cca0014a:00003","en":"Taichi: \"I'm giving you this.\"","verdict":"acceptable","categories":["presentation"]}]},{"ref":"ccfc:sn:0063:00000149:text","row":15355,"ordinal":4,"kind":"text","jp":"朝のサンドイッチを差し出す。","en":"I held out my breakfast sandwich.","speakerJa":"","speakerEn":"","ghs":[{"id":"ghs-tl:finding:001980","unitId":"ghs-tl:cca0014a:00004","en":"I present her with the sandwich from this morning.","verdict":"acceptable","categories":["presentation"]}]},{"ref":"ccfc:sn:0063:000001de:text","row":15356,"ordinal":5,"kind":"text","jp":"ぽかんと、見つめる冬子。","en":"Touko stared at it blankly.","speakerJa":"","speakerEn":"","ghs":[{"id":"ghs-tl:finding:001981","unitId":"ghs-tl:cca0014a:00005","en":"Touko gazes at it, flabbergasted.","verdict":"acceptable","categories":["word_choice"]}]},{"ref":"ccfc:sn:0063:00000233:text","row":15357,"ordinal":6,"kind":"text","jp":"「なに、コレ」","en":"“What’s this?”","speakerJa":"冬子","speakerEn":"Touko","ghs":[{"id":"ghs-tl:finding:001982","unitId":"ghs-tl:cca0014a:00006","en":"Touko: \"What's this, even?\"","verdict":"acceptable","categories":["word_choice"]}]},{"ref":"ccfc:sn:0063:00000261:text","row":15358,"ordinal":7,"kind":"text","jp":"「あんまん」","en":"“A red-bean bun.”","speakerJa":"太一","speakerEn":"Taichi","ghs":[{"id":"ghs-tl:finding:001983","unitId":"ghs-tl:cca0014a:00007","en":"Taichi: \"Anman.\"","verdict":"confirmed_error","categories":["undertranslation","word_choice"],"assessment":"The source names a common sweet bean bun. Leaving the food name as unexplained romanized Japanese withholds ordinary lexical content from the English reader.","remedy":"Render the food as a sweet bean bun or otherwise supply its ordinary English sense.","highlights":[{"color":"red","end":14,"start":9,"text":"Anman"}]}]},{"ref":"ccfc:sn:0063:0000030b:text","row":15359,"ordinal":8,"kind":"text","jp":"「んなわけないでしょ！！　サンドイッチでしょ！」","en":"“No way!! It’s a sandwich!”","speakerJa":"冬子","speakerEn":"Touko","ghs":[{"id":"ghs-tl:finding:001984","unitId":"ghs-tl:cca0014a:00008","en":"Touko: \"'s not that at all you know!!! It's a sandwich you know!\"","verdict":"confirmed_error","categories":["grammar","register_voice"],"assessment":"The clipped Japanese opening is colloquial but grammatical in context. The English begins with a stranded contraction and adds a repeated tag, producing malformed dialogue rather than equivalent conversational compression.","remedy":"Use a grammatical emphatic denial before identifying it as a sandwich.","highlights":[{"color":"red","end":35,"start":8,"text":"'s not that at all you know"}]}]},{"ref":"ccfc:sn:0063:0000035b:text","row":15360,"ordinal":9,"kind":"text","jp":"「知ってるじゃないか」","en":"“See? You knew.”","speakerJa":"太一","speakerEn":"Taichi","ghs":[{"id":"ghs-tl:finding:001985","unitId":"ghs-tl:cca0014a:00009","en":"Taichi: \"So you do know don't you.\"","verdict":"acceptable","categories":["word_choice"]}]},{"ref":"ccfc:sn:0063:00000391:text","row":15361,"ordinal":10,"kind":"text","jp":"「ほれ」","en":"“Here.”","speakerJa":"太一","speakerEn":"Taichi","ghs":[{"id":"ghs-tl:finding:001986","unitId":"ghs-tl:cca0014a:00010","en":"Taichi: \"Have it.\"","verdict":"acceptable","categories":["word_choice"]}]},{"ref":"ccfc:sn:0063:000003b1:text","row":15362,"ordinal":11,"kind":"text","jp":"ずい","en":"I thrust it toward her.","speakerJa":"","speakerEn":"","ghs":[{"id":"ghs-tl:finding:001987","unitId":"ghs-tl:cca0014a:00011","en":"Slid over,","verdict":"acceptable","categories":["word_choice"]}]},{"ref":"ccfc:sn:0063:00000453:text","row":15363,"ordinal":12,"kind":"text","jp":"「……やめて」","en":"“...Stop.”","speakerJa":"冬子","speakerEn":"Touko","ghs":[{"id":"ghs-tl:finding:001988","unitId":"ghs-tl:cca0014a:00012","en":"Touko: \"...stop this.\"","verdict":"acceptable","categories":["word_choice"]}]},{"ref":"ccfc:sn:0063:00000479:text","row":15364,"ordinal":13,"kind":"text","jp":"手を払われる。","en":"She swatted my hand away.","speakerJa":"","speakerEn":"","ghs":[{"id":"ghs-tl:finding:001989","unitId":"ghs-tl:cca0014a:00013","en":"a swat of her hands,","verdict":"confirmed_error","categories":["mistranslation","word_choice"],"assessment":"The passive source says the narrator has his hand brushed or knocked aside. The English instead describes an indeterminate swat involving her hands and loses the affected hand and action direction.","remedy":"State that she bats or brushes his hand away.","highlights":[{"color":"red","end":19,"start":0,"text":"a swat of her hands"}]}]},{"ref":"ccfc:sn:0063:0000049f:text","row":15365,"ordinal":14,"kind":"text","jp":"サンドイッチが落ちた。","en":"The sandwich fell.","speakerJa":"","speakerEn":"","ghs":[{"id":"ghs-tl:finding:001990","unitId":"ghs-tl:cca0014a:00014","en":"the sandwich fell,","verdict":"acceptable","categories":["word_choice"]}]},{"ref":"ccfc:sn:0063:000004cd:text","row":15366,"ordinal":15,"kind":"text","jp":"拾う。","en":"I picked it up.","speakerJa":"","speakerEn":"","ghs":[{"id":"ghs-tl:finding:001991","unitId":"ghs-tl:cca0014a:00015","en":"recovered.","verdict":"confirmed_error","categories":["undertranslation","word_choice"],"assessment":"The source is the concrete action of picking the fallen item up. The English substitutes an abstract result and omits the visible retrieval action.","remedy":"Render the action directly as picking it up.","highlights":[{"color":"red","end":9,"start":0,"text":"recovered"}]}]},{"ref":"ccfc:sn:0063:000004f3:text","row":15367,"ordinal":16,"kind":"text","jp":"「ちゃんと食べてるのか？」","en":"“Have you been eating properly?”","speakerJa":"太一","speakerEn":"Taichi","ghs":[{"id":"ghs-tl:finding:001992","unitId":"ghs-tl:cca0014a:00016","en":"Taichi: \"Are you eating properly?\"","verdict":"acceptable","categories":["word_choice"]}]},{"ref":"ccfc:sn:0063:000005ab:text","row":15368,"ordinal":17,"kind":"text","jp":"「あんたに、関係ない」","en":"“None of your business.”","speakerJa":"冬子","speakerEn":"Touko","ghs":[{"id":"ghs-tl:finding:001993","unitId":"ghs-tl:cca0014a:00017","en":"Touko: \"That's... none of yer business.\"","verdict":"confirmed_error","categories":["addition","register_voice"],"assessment":"The source is blunt and casual but carries no marked regional dialect. The English adds conspicuous dialect spelling that changes the character's voice.","remedy":"Keep the curt refusal without invented dialect.","highlights":[{"color":"red","end":29,"start":26,"text":"yer"}]}]},{"ref":"ccfc:sn:0063:000005d9:text","row":15369,"ordinal":18,"kind":"text","jp":"そっぽを向く。","en":"She turned away.","speakerJa":"","speakerEn":"","ghs":[{"id":"ghs-tl:finding:001994","unitId":"ghs-tl:cca0014a:00018","en":"Uncooperative.","verdict":"confirmed_error","categories":["mistranslation","undertranslation"],"assessment":"The source narrates the physical action of turning her face away. The English replaces that action with the narrator's evaluative label.","remedy":"State that she turns away.","highlights":[{"color":"red","end":13,"start":0,"text":"Uncooperative"}]}]},{"ref":"ccfc:sn:0063:00000607:text","row":15370,"ordinal":19,"kind":"text","jp":"「自分しか、自分の心配をしてくれる人間がいないのは、つらいだろ？」","en":"“It’s hard when you’re the only one looking out for yourself, isn’t it?”","speakerJa":"太一","speakerEn":"Taichi","ghs":[{"id":"ghs-tl:finding:001995","unitId":"ghs-tl:cca0014a:00019","en":"Taichi: \"Having no human alive, none outside of you, that worry about you... it's painful, right?\"","verdict":"confirmed_error","categories":["addition","grammar"],"assessment":"The source says it is painful when nobody but oneself will worry about oneself. The English adds the absolute claim that no human is alive, then damages the relation with a subject-verb agreement error.","remedy":"Express that being the only person who worries about oneself is painful.","highlights":[{"color":"red","end":73,"start":9,"text":"Having no human alive, none outside of you, that worry about you"}]}]},{"ref":"ccfc:sn:0063:00000686:text","row":15371,"ordinal":20,"kind":"text","jp":"「何言ってるのかわからない」","en":"“I don’t know what you’re talking about.”","speakerJa":"冬子","speakerEn":"Touko","ghs":[{"id":"ghs-tl:finding:001996","unitId":"ghs-tl:cca0014a:00020","en":"Touko: \"What's that even mean I don't know.\"","verdict":"confirmed_error","categories":["grammar"],"assessment":"The source is a direct statement that she does not understand what he is saying. The English splices a question and declaration without the syntax needed to connect them.","remedy":"Use a grammatical equivalent such as 'I don't know what you're talking about.'","highlights":[{"color":"red","end":42,"start":8,"text":"What's that even mean I don't know"}]}]},{"ref":"ccfc:sn:0063:000006c2:text","row":15372,"ordinal":21,"kind":"text","jp":"「人に心配されたい」","en":"“You want someone to worry about you.”","speakerJa":"太一","speakerEn":"Taichi","ghs":[{"id":"ghs-tl:finding:001997","unitId":"ghs-tl:cca0014a:00021","en":"Taichi: \"You want people to worry about you.\"","verdict":"acceptable","categories":["word_choice"]}]},{"ref":"ccfc:sn:0063:000006f6:text","row":15373,"ordinal":22,"kind":"text","jp":"「満たされたい」","en":"“You want to feel fulfilled.”","speakerJa":"太一","speakerEn":"Taichi","ghs":[{"id":"ghs-tl:finding:001998","unitId":"ghs-tl:cca0014a:00022","en":"Taichi: \"You want to be fulfilled.\"","verdict":"acceptable","categories":["word_choice"]}]},{"ref":"ccfc:sn:0063:00000743:text","row":15374,"ordinal":23,"kind":"text","jp":"「……」","en":"“……”","speakerJa":"冬子","speakerEn":"Touko","ghs":[{"id":"ghs-tl:finding:001999","unitId":"ghs-tl:cca0014a:00023","en":"Touko: \"...\"","verdict":"acceptable","categories":["word_choice"]}]},{"ref":"ccfc:sn:0063:0000076b:text","row":15375,"ordinal":24,"kind":"text","jp":"「俺、ちょっとは心配なんだけどな」","en":"“I do worry about you. A little.”","speakerJa":"太一","speakerEn":"Taichi","ghs":[{"id":"ghs-tl:finding:002000","unitId":"ghs-tl:cca0014a:00024","en":"Taichi: \"And me, I'm getting somewhat worried here.\"","verdict":"acceptable","categories":["word_choice"]}]},{"ref":"ccfc:sn:0063:00000806:text","row":15376,"ordinal":25,"kind":"text","jp":"きっと俺を睨む。","en":"She glared straight at me.","speakerJa":"","speakerEn":"","ghs":[{"id":"ghs-tl:finding:002001","unitId":"ghs-tl:cca0014a:00025","en":"She sternly glares at me.","verdict":"acceptable","categories":["word_choice"]}]},{"ref":"ccfc:sn:0063:000008b4:text","row":15377,"ordinal":26,"kind":"text","jp":"「よく、言う」","en":"“That’s rich.”","speakerJa":"冬子","speakerEn":"Touko","ghs":[{"id":"ghs-tl:finding:002002","unitId":"ghs-tl:cca0014a:00026","en":"Touko: \"Look... who's talking.\"","verdict":"acceptable","categories":["word_choice"]}]},{"ref":"ccfc:sn:0063:00000960:text","row":15378,"ordinal":27,"kind":"text","jp":"「心配してるなら、どうして、どうしてっ！」","en":"“If you’re worried, then why—why?!”","speakerJa":"冬子","speakerEn":"Touko","ghs":[{"id":"ghs-tl:finding:002003","unitId":"ghs-tl:cca0014a:00027","en":"Touko: \"If you're worried, then why, why!\"","verdict":"acceptable","categories":["word_choice"]}]},{"ref":"ccfc:sn:0063:000009a2:text","row":15379,"ordinal":28,"kind":"text","jp":"いきり立つ。","en":"She flared up.","speakerJa":"","speakerEn":"","ghs":[{"id":"ghs-tl:finding:002004","unitId":"ghs-tl:cca0014a:00028","en":"She loses her temper.","verdict":"acceptable","categories":["word_choice"]}]},{"ref":"ccfc:sn:0063:000009ce:text","row":15380,"ordinal":29,"kind":"text","jp":"「……桐原」","en":"“...Kirihara.”","speakerJa":"太一","speakerEn":"Taichi","ghs":[{"id":"ghs-tl:finding:002005","unitId":"ghs-tl:cca0014a:00029","en":"Taichi: \"...Kirihara.\"","verdict":"acceptable","categories":["word_choice"]}]},{"ref":"ccfc:sn:0063:00000a17:text","row":15381,"ordinal":30,"kind":"text","jp":"「なによ！」","en":"“What?!”","speakerJa":"冬子","speakerEn":"Touko","ghs":[{"id":"ghs-tl:finding:002006","unitId":"ghs-tl:cca0014a:00030","en":"Touko: \"What now!\"","verdict":"acceptable","categories":["word_choice"]}]},{"ref":"ccfc:sn:0063:00000a43:text","row":15382,"ordinal":31,"kind":"text","jp":"「顔色悪いな。生理か？」","en":"“You look pale. Are you on your period?”","speakerJa":"太一","speakerEn":"Taichi","ghs":[{"id":"ghs-tl:finding:002007","unitId":"ghs-tl:cca0014a:00031","en":"Taichi: \"Your face looks off-color. Menses?\"","verdict":"confirmed_error","categories":["word_choice","register_voice"],"assessment":"The source bluntly asks whether her poor complexion is due to her period. 'Off-color' is semantically distracting in English and the isolated clinical noun 'Menses?' does not function as the same direct question.","remedy":"Use a plain question about looking pale and being on her period.","highlights":[{"color":"red","end":42,"start":25,"text":"off-color. Menses"}]}]},{"ref":"ccfc:sn:0063:00000b62:text","row":15383,"ordinal":32,"kind":"text","jp":"びたーん！","en":"WHAP!","speakerJa":"","speakerEn":"","ghs":[{"id":"ghs-tl:finding:002008","unitId":"ghs-tl:cca0014a:00032","en":"Smaaack!","verdict":"acceptable","categories":["word_choice"]}]},{"ref":"ccfc:sn:0063:00000ba9:text","row":15384,"ordinal":33,"kind":"text","jp":"「馬鹿じゃないの！」","en":"“Are you stupid?!”","speakerJa":"冬子","speakerEn":"Touko","ghs":[{"id":"ghs-tl:finding:002009","unitId":"ghs-tl:cca0014a:00033","en":"Touko: \"Aren't you stupid!\"","verdict":"confirmed_error","categories":["grammar","register_voice"],"assessment":"The source is an angry exclamatory insult, not an information-seeking negative question. The English question form conflicts with its exclamation punctuation and weakens the speech act.","remedy":"Use a direct exclamation such as 'You idiot!'","highlights":[{"color":"red","end":25,"start":8,"text":"Aren't you stupid"}]}]},{"ref":"ccfc:sn:0063:00000cb7:text","row":15385,"ordinal":34,"kind":"text","jp":"呪詛を吐いて、出て行く。","en":"She spat the curse and stormed out.","speakerJa":"","speakerEn":"","ghs":[{"id":"ghs-tl:finding:002010","unitId":"ghs-tl:cca0014a:00034","en":"That curse spat out, she leaves.","verdict":"confirmed_error","categories":["grammar","mistranslation"],"assessment":"The source says she spits out a curse and leaves. The English absolute construction is malformed and obscures who performs the spitting.","remedy":"Make her the agent of both actions in a grammatical sentence.","highlights":[{"color":"red","end":31,"start":0,"text":"That curse spat out, she leaves"}]}]},{"ref":"ccfc:sn:0063:00000cef:text","row":15386,"ordinal":35,"kind":"text","jp":"「あ、サンドイッチ……」","en":"“Oh—the sandwich...”","speakerJa":"太一","speakerEn":"Taichi","ghs":[{"id":"ghs-tl:finding:002011","unitId":"ghs-tl:cca0014a:00035","en":"Taichi: \"Ah, the sandwich...\"","verdict":"acceptable","categories":["word_choice"]}]},{"ref":"ccfc:sn:0063:00000d1f:text","row":15387,"ordinal":36,"kind":"text","jp":"ため息。","en":"I sighed.","speakerJa":"","speakerEn":"","ghs":[{"id":"ghs-tl:finding:002012","unitId":"ghs-tl:cca0014a:00036","en":"I sigh.","verdict":"acceptable","categories":["word_choice"]}]},{"ref":"ccfc:sn:0063:00000d47:text","row":15388,"ordinal":37,"kind":"text","jp":"「……あんまいい死に方できないぞ」","en":"“...You’re going to meet a bad end.”","speakerJa":"太一","speakerEn":"Taichi","ghs":[{"id":"ghs-tl:finding:002013","unitId":"ghs-tl:cca0014a:00037","en":"Taichi: \"...that ain't a really good way to die ya know.\"","verdict":"confirmed_error","categories":["idiom_calque","mistranslation"],"assessment":"The source warns that she will not come to a good end or die well. The English recasts the conduct itself as a method of dying and adds marked dialect.","remedy":"Render the warning as not coming to a good end.","highlights":[{"color":"red","end":55,"start":12,"text":"that ain't a really good way to die ya know"}]}]},{"ref":"ccfc:sn:0063:00000d81:text","row":15389,"ordinal":38,"kind":"text","jp":"仕方ないので、包みをといて自分でかぶりついた。","en":"With no other choice, I unwrapped it and took a bite myself.","speakerJa":"","speakerEn":"","ghs":[{"id":"ghs-tl:finding:002014","unitId":"ghs-tl:cca0014a:00038","en":"Nothing I can do, so I undid the wrapping and bit into it myself.","verdict":"acceptable","categories":["word_choice"]}]}]}
